  blurb:"Crash Team Racing Nitro-Fueled running natively on Windows. It's a fork of SacredFire, the native Linux port: the PS4 game's own x86-64 code runs directly on your CPU, with a small runtime standing in for the PS4's system libraries and a shadPS4-based renderer on Vulkan. Includes a full launcher, modern upscalers and ultrawide support.",
  status:"<b>Playable on Windows:</b> menus, Adventure and Arcade, races, sound, cutscenes, saves and DLC. The developer reports 110–130 fps uncapped on an RTX 3070. First-time shaders cause short stalls until they're cached. <b>Online play is being worked on</b> (a private-server path) but isn't usable yet. You need your own decrypted dump of the USA (CUSA13795) or EU (CUSA14876) edition with update 1.21. <b>No commits since Oct 19.</b>",
